<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mattathias</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 166 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mattathias was a Jewish priest of Modein who, according to the First Book of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maccabees">Maccabees</a>, began the revolt against the Seleucid king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iv-epiphanes">Antiochus IV</a> in 167 BCE by killing a Jew who sacrificed to the Greek gods and the king's officer who ordered it. He fled to the hills with his five sons, the Maccabees, and died about a year later, leaving command to Judas.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mattathias.jpg" alt="Mattathias" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges Reverdy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mattathias_medal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
